-- ============================================================
-- Seed data : static reference data
--   films (24) / cinemas (8) / halls (40) / coupon templates (3)
--
-- Schedules (~1400) and schedule_seat (~168k rows) are NOT created
-- here - they are generated programmatically by admin-service:
--   POST /admin/demo/generate-schedule
--
-- Test user accounts are also created by user-service at startup
-- (DemoDataInitializer), so that the BCrypt hashes are guaranteed
-- to match the encoder configured in the application. Hard-coding a
-- BCrypt hash in SQL risks a hash that no encoder will ever verify.
--
-- Fixed id ranges used by seed data (snowflake ids are far larger,
-- so there is no collision risk):
--   films          1001-1024
--   cinemas        2001-2008
--   halls          3001-3040
--   coupon tpl     4001-4003
-- ============================================================

